UI-T01 | Publish tokens as the single source: tokens.css packaged, token lint bans raw hex and magic pixel values outside it | - | S | design/tokens.css is consumed through one package entry; lint fails on raw hex in any component stylesheet | token lint fixtures; contrast audit on both themes
UI-T02 | Theme runtime: OS default, stored preference with safe fallback, no flash, profile persistence hook | UI-T01 | S | Dark OS with no preference loads dark with no flash; blocked storage does not throw; the preference is saved through a port once sign-in exists | unit tests with storage stubbed; no-flash check in browser test
UI-T03 | Front-end binding decision (ADR) and wrapper conventions that reuse the CSS classes | K0-T01, UI-T01 | S | ADR accepted; wrappers map 1 to 1 to the documented classes and never fork the look | review only
UI-T04 | Buttons and form controls: variants, sizes, busy and disabled states, field, error and hint patterns | UI-T03 | M | Every state in the reference page renders from the library; errors are announced through aria-describedby; one primary per view lint | component tests; axe; lint fixture with 2 primaries
UI-T05 | Menus: action menu, single select, searchable list, split button; keyboard, outside click, edge alignment | UI-T03 | M | Enter, arrows, Home, End, Escape and Tab behave per the spec; over 8 items adds search and scrolls at 320 px; right-edge menus stay inside the viewport | keyboard tests on 6 keys; axe; visual test at 1280 px
UI-T06 | Overlays: modal, toast with undo, side panel, banner; focus trap and return | UI-T04 | M | Focus stays inside an open modal and returns to the trigger; destructive action is never the default focus; toasts are announced politely | keyboard and screen-reader tests; axe
UI-T07 | App shell: global header, rail with pinned views and counts, tab bar, utility bar, responsive collapse | UI-T05 | M | Rail collapses to 48 px under 1100 px and to a menu under 720 px; skip link reaches main; header actions follow the placement table | responsive screenshots at 1440, 1280, 1024 and 720 px; keyboard pass
UI-T08 | Page templates: dashboard, list, record, settings with the 12-column no-gap grid | UI-T07 | M | Every grid row spans 12 of 12; cards in a row are equal height; no horizontal scroll at 1280 px | screenshot baselines in both themes; grid-sum lint
UI-T09 | Data table: sticky header, sort, selection, bulk bar, row menu, pager, density toggle, truncation | UI-T05, UI-T08 | M | Selection count is announced; row actions sit in the last column; compact density gives 26 px rows; 10,000 rows page at 25 per page | component and keyboard tests; axe; performance check on 10,000 rows
UI-T10 | Charts: token colours, one accent series at most, text alternative for every chart | UI-T08 | S | Each chart has a caption or hidden table; series are distinguishable without colour; axis labels are 11 px | contrast check on series; axe
UI-T11 | Secure data display: masked fields with audited reveal, session-expiry and 401 handling, no-permission and error states | UI-T09, K7-T06 | M | Masked field shows the last 4 characters; reveal writes 1 sensitive-read audit row; a 401 returns to sign-in with 0 tokens or personal data in browser storage | integration test with the audit fake; storage inspection test
UI-T12 | Design gates in CI: contrast audit, colour budget, no inline style, no raw hex, grid-sum lint | UI-T01 | M | A failing pair, a budget breach, an inline style or a raw hex each fail the build with the file named | one failing fixture per gate
UI-T13 | Accessibility scan and screenshot comparison in both themes for all templates | UI-T08, UI-T12 | M | 0 serious or critical axe violations on 4 templates in 2 themes; screenshot diff under 0.1% against baselines | CI run on the reference templates
UI-T14 | Tenant branding: logo, product name and accent with save-time contrast validation | UI-T04, K1-T09 | S | An accent that fails 4.5:1 with midnight text or matches the danger hue is rejected with the reason; changes are audited | unit tests on the validator; audit-fake assertion
